k in support of  many the estate of Donald Windham the  office of the university president the  office of development the director and  staff of the by Nicki and the prize  steering committee each deserve thanks  for working to develop and implement a  process that is as rigorous as it is  fair as focused on excellence as it is  global in reach and with that I'd like  to introduce president-elect Peter  salafi who will read the winners of the  first Windham Campbell prizes thank you  very much Michael thank you all for  being here today for essentially a  historic announcement since this is the  first Windham Campbell Prize  announcement and I'm delighted to be  here for this historical occasion as  well so yell is a place that hopes to  inspire and recognize greatness in every  field and the wyndham Campbell prizes  allow us to fulfill that ambition in the  field of world literature in ways we are  only beginning to understand i'm  particularly looking forward to our  prize winners joining us for the  literary festival in September the  festival will be a boon to the  intellectual and educational mission of  the University and as Michael said we're  deeply indebted to Donald Windham and  Sandy Campbell for creating this legacy  this is a global writers prize which  supports writers at all stages of their  careers in the practice of their craft  the individuals that we recognize today  are inspiring to us as artists of the  first order and it is truly excited to  provide these authors with the means to  develop their work in ways that will  benefit all of us who love to read so I  look forward to the dialogue these  winners will inspire on the el campus  and around the world especially when  they come here this fall are we ready  the winners of the window campbell  prizes for fiction are awarded to james  salter Tom McCarthy and Zoe Wickham for  nonfiction the winners are Adina Hoffman  Johnny Steinberg and Jeremy scale for  drama the winners are nami wallace  steph